## Request

Qualify the exact Codex App Server `0.153.0` runtime as a separate campaign. Preserve the existing
operator-runtime trust contract: positive qualification is reviewed diagnostic and optional strict-
certification evidence, not a new normal-mode admission gate. Use the disposable Tool Shed Linux and
Windows test beds, and do not infer one platform's result from the other.

Exercise the supported Sol/high planning, Terra/low verification, and Terra/medium bounded CAMP
roles through their real App Server paths. Record exact executable identities and content-free
evidence. Treat unavailable packages, protocol differences, unsafe mutation, unexpected paths,
failed deterministic verification, missing terminal dispatch state, or authentication/model
failures as explicit blockers rather than inherited qualification.

If qualification exposes a Tool Shed or Codex compatibility defect, preserve the evidence and
route the repair as separately scoped work before changing product behavior. This campaign does not
authorize deployment, publication, release, API-key fallback, broader writing roles, or production
workloads.

